[
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "Debt Limit City Charter Language Change",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      },
      {
        "type": "linebreak",
        "version": 1
      },
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "Shall Section 97 of the Boulder Home Rule Charter be amended pursuant to Ordinance 8762 to modify the City's debt limitation to be not more than three percent of the actual value of the taxable property within the City?",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "extended-quote",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "Who put the measure on the ballot?",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "extended-heading",
    "version": 1,
    "tag": "h2"
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "City of Boulder Issue 2M was placed on the ballot by the Boulder City Council through ",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "detail": 0,
            "format": 0,
            "mode": "normal",
            "style": "",
            "text": "Ordinance 8762",
            "type": "extended-text",
            "version": 1
          }
        ],
        "direction": "ltr",
        "format": "",
        "indent": 0,
        "type": "link",
        "version": 1,
        "rel": "noreferrer",
        "target": null,
        "title": null,
        "url": "https://documents.bouldercolorado.gov/WebLink/DocView.aspx?id=203851&dbid=0&repo=LF8PROD2"
      },
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": ".",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "paragraph",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "Short Description:",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "extended-heading",
    "version": 1,
    "tag": "h2"
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "Amends the city charter so Boulder's debt limit is calculated as no more than three percent of the actual value of taxable property rather than assessed value. The city asserts this is consistent with how most municipalities and the state calculate debt limitation.",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "paragraph",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "Analysis and Commentary:",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "extended-heading",
    "version": 1,
    "tag": "h2"
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "Support. City of Boulder Issue 2M was placed on the ballot by the Boulder City Council through ",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "detail": 0,
            "format": 8,
            "mode": "normal",
            "style": "",
            "text": "Ordinance 8762",
            "type": "extended-text",
            "version": 1
          }
        ],
        "direction": "ltr",
        "format": "",
        "indent": 0,
        "type": "link",
        "version": 1,
        "rel": null,
        "target": null,
        "title": null,
        "url": "https://documents.bouldercolorado.gov/WebLink/DocView.aspx?id=203851&dbid=0&repo=LF8PROD2"
      },
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": ".",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "paragraph",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "The City of Boulder is looking to update its charter to allow a more reasonable amount of debt to be authorized in order to pursue future projects. Note that this ballot measure does not authorize any new debt itself, which must be authorized through a specific ballot question.",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "paragraph",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "City Debt Limitation Charter Amendment (Attachment D - Ord. 8762) This measure would amend Charter Sec. 97 so that debt limitation could be no more than the “actual value” (rather than the “assessed value” as currently written) of the taxable property within the city. This amendment would bring the city’s charter in line with all other Boulder County communities and state statute. ",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "paragraph",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "detail": 0,
            "format": 8,
            "mode": "normal",
            "style": "",
            "text": "August 6th Agenda Packet, Boulder City Council",
            "type": "extended-text",
            "version": 1
          }
        ],
        "direction": "ltr",
        "format": "",
        "indent": 0,
        "type": "link",
        "version": 1,
        "rel": null,
        "target": null,
        "title": null,
        "url": "https://documents.bouldercolorado.gov/WebLink/DocView.aspx?id=202624&dbid=0&repo=LF8PROD2"
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "paragraph",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "Boulder County has a useful ",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "detail": 0,
            "format": 8,
            "mode": "normal",
            "style": "",
            "text": "terminology web page",
            "type": "extended-text",
            "version": 1
          }
        ],
        "direction": "ltr",
        "format": "",
        "indent": 0,
        "type": "link",
        "version": 1,
        "rel": null,
        "target": null,
        "title": null,
        "url": "https://bouldercounty.gov/property-and-land/assessor/appeals/nod-glossary/"
      },
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": ":",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "paragraph",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "Actual Value is “That value determined by appropriate consideration of the cost approach, the market approach, and the income approach to appraisal.”",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "paragraph",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "The assessed value is typically much lower, and determined by this formula: Assessed Value = Actual Value x Assessment Rate. The assessment rate is typically a fixed amount, i.e. 6.7% to determine what is taxable.",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "paragraph",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "So in practice, the actual value is a significantly higher number and more reflective of a reasonable bonding amount — a maximum of 3% of the entire property value of all structures in the city.",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "paragraph",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "Again, an important caveat — Measure 2M does not take on any new debt, and such debt must be authorized through other ballot measures.",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "paragraph",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "The change to the city’s debt limitation would have no fiscal impact, but would allow the city to issue general obligation bonds above the current charter limitation of three percent of the assessed value of the taxable property within the city. Assessed value as of 2025 for Boulder is $5.0 billion. Based on the most recent assessed value, the city is limited to $150.7 million in general obligation debt.",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "extended-quote",
    "version": 1
  },
